An inquiry into the drink that each of the $60$ Year $8$ students brings to school set the hypothesis "water is brought by more than half of Year $8$ students". The collected data is displayed below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.72]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,11.4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(11.2,0);
\foreach \y in {10,20,30} {\draw (-0.2,\y/3)--(0,\y/3); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,\y/3) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.2,0) {$0$};
\draw (0.8,0) rectangle (2.3,10.33);
\draw (3.1,0) rectangle (4.6,4.0);
\draw (5.4,0) rectangle (6.9,3.0);
\draw (7.7,0) rectangle (9.2,2.67);
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1.55,0) {Water};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3.85,0) {Juice};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6.15,0) {Milk};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (8.45,0) {Cordial};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.4,5) {Number of students};
\node[below] at (5.0,-1.0) {Drink brought};
\node at (5.0,11.1) {Drinks brought};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which conclusion should the report state?

An inquiry asked $19$ Year $8$ students in one class how many sports they play outside school, and set the hypothesis "most Year $8$ students at the school play at least two sports outside school". The collected data is displayed below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-0.6,0)--(7.4,0);
\foreach \x in {0,1,2,3,4,5,6} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \x/\c in {0/2,1/5,2/6,3/3,4/2,6/1} {\foreach \k in {1,...,\c} {\fill (\x,{0.35*\k}) circle (2.2pt);}}
\node[below] at (3,-0.9) {Sports played outside school};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement should the report make?
